{
  "id": "Lyo.ClamAv.Client",
  "name": "Lyo.ClamAv.Client",
  "area": "Integration",
  "tagline": "HTTP client for a self-hosted clamav-rest scan service.",
  "description": "HTTP client for a self-hosted [clamav-rest](https://github.com/solita/clamav-rest) service. `ClamAvClient` subclasses `LyoHttpClient`.\n\n**Archetype C (vendor client).** The host points `BaseUrl` at the service (for example `http://127.0.0.1:8080/`). This package does not talk to clamd's INSTREAM socket.\n\n`ScanAsync` posts the stream as multipart field `file`. A body status of `OK` is clean. `FOUND` is infected and `description` is the signature. clamav-rest returns HTTP 406 for a hit; that response is still a verdict. Any other non-success status throws `LyoHttpException`. `GetVersionAsync` reads the plain-text `version` endpoint.",
  "features": [
    "**Scan.** `POST {BaseUrl}/scan` via `PostFileAsAsync`. The part name is `file`.",
    "**Verdicts.** `OK` → clean. `FOUND` → infected, signature from `description`. Any other JSON status → error. HTTP 406 is read as a verdict.",
    "**Version.** `GET {BaseUrl}/version` returns the trimmed engine version string.",
    "**Registration.** `AddClamAvClient`, the options instance overload, and `AddClamAvClientFromConfiguration`. Also registers transient `IClamAvClient`."
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Register",
      "language": "csharp",
      "code": "services.AddClamAvClient(o => o.BaseUrl = \"http://127.0.0.1:8080/\");\n\nservices.AddClamAvClientFromConfiguration(configuration);"
    },
    {
      "title": "Scan a stream",
      "language": "csharp",
      "code": "var result = await client.ScanAsync(stream, \"upload.bin\", ct);\nif (result.Status == ClamScanStatus.Infected)\n    Console.WriteLine(result.Signature);"
    }
  ],
